The building official shall have the authority to appoint qualified inspectors and permit staff to allow for the efficient operation of the building services department, within budgetary constraints as approved by the mayor and council.
Qualified inspectors and permit staff shall mean the following:
(1) A person inspecting for compliance with the International Building Code or the portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a building inspector;
(2) A person inspecting for compliance with the National Electrical Code or the electrical portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a Residential Electrical Inspector or an electrical contractor license from the State Construction Industry Licensing Board;
(3) A person inspecting for compliance of nonresidential buildings with the National Electrical Code who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a Commercial Electrical Inspector or an electrical contractor license from the State Construction Industry Licensing Board;
(4) A person inspecting for compliance with the International Fuel Gas Code who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a Mechanical or Plumbing Inspector or a conditioned air contractor, journeyman plumber, or master plumber license from the State Construction Industry Licensing Board;
(5) A person inspecting for compliance with the International Mechanical Code or the mechanical portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a mechanical inspector or a conditioned air contractor license from the state construction industry licensing board;
(6) A person inspecting for compliance with the International Plumbing Code or the plumbing portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a Plumbing Inspector or a journeyman plumber or master plumber license from the State Construction Licensing Board;
(7) A person inspecting for compliance with any portion of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a one and two-family dwelling inspector;
(8) A person inspecting for compliance with the Georgia Accessibility Code who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as an accessibility inspector;
(9) A person inspecting for compliance with the International Property Maintenance Code who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a property maintenance and housing inspector;
(10) A person receiving or issuing permits who holds certification from the International Code Council (ICC) as a permit technician;
A qualified inspector shall be empowered to perform any inspection required by the applicable codes including but not limited to inspections for footings, foundations, concrete slabs, framing, electrical, plumbing, heating ventilation and air conditioning (HVAC), or any and all other inspections necessary or required for the issuance of a certificate of occupancy or completion.
(Ord. No. 2006-06, § 1(18-32), 2-21-06)

